        },
        "faq_item_R33MaN": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do you prepare HiPP Organic formula?",
            "answer": "<p>To prepare HiPP formula, follow these guidelines:</p><ul><li>Use the scoop provided in the pack. Don’t use any other scoop or measuring device.</li><li>Don’t alter the strength of the formula by adding extra water or scoops. Follow the recommended quantity of water and measuring spoon specified for each stage.</li><li>For hygiene reasons, always prepare fresh feeds and avoid preparing them in advance. Use the prepared formula within 2 hours. Discard any leftover formula after feeding.</li><li>Don’t heat the formula in a microwave, as it may create hot spots and cause scalding. Use alternative methods for warming the formula, such as a bottle warmer or warm water bath.</li><li>Introduce a cup or beaker as soon as possible to prevent prolonged or frequent contact of teeth with milk feeds, which can increase the risk of tooth decay.</li><li>Use the sachet of formula within 3 weeks of opening to ensure freshness and quality.</li></ul><p>By following these instructions, you can ensure the proper preparation and safety of HiPP formula for your baby's consumption.</p>"
          }
        },
